# Test-run artifacts — never commit these.
#
# The sharness-style harness (test-lib.sh) runs each test inside a per-PID
# `trash.$$` working directory and removes it on exit, but stray or older runs
# can leave repo working directories behind here. The stress suite
# (t0700-stress-extreme.sh) also builds throwaway repos directly in CWD — one of
# them, `extreme-path-test`, created a 600+ character path that exceeds the
# Windows MAX_PATH limit and broke `git checkout`/`git clone` on Windows (so no
# win32 binary could ever be published). None of this belongs in version control.
/trash.*/
/test-results/
/test-repo/

# All stress/QA scratch repos are generated at runtime; ignore the whole tree.
/*-test/
